\begin_layout Subsection
Optical modeling
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Note Note
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The dielectric function for Ti is taken from 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citet
key "Golosov2011"

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\end_inset

Generally, we use dielectric function given by applying the Drude approximation
 to the electron gas and obtain 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "Dresselhaus2001"

\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\varepsilon=\varepsilon_{\infty}-\frac{\omega_{p}^{2}}{\omega^{2}}\frac{1}{1+i\frac{\nu}{\omega}}\label{eq:DielectricFunction}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\omega_{p}^{2}=\frac{n_{e}e^{2}}{m_{e}m^{*}\varepsilon_{0}}
\]

\end_inset

Parameters are detailed in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:DielectricFunctions"

\end_inset

.
 
