\begin_layout Section
Far sub-wavelength SPP modes in multilayer systems
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Periodicity of SPP at single interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Periodicity calculations have been performed for possible combinations between
 the following interfaces: water, excited water, Si, excited Si, and amorphous
 Si.
 Periodicity of SPPs at 
\begin_inset Formula $Water/a-Si^{*}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $a-Si^{*}/Si$
\end_inset

 interfaces have been performed by 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citet
key "Miyaji2012"

\end_inset

 and will be used in the next sections.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
However, calculations had not been performed for excited water interface
 with Si.
 This case is interesting and can lead to generation far subwavelength LSFL
 ripples perpendicular to the polarization as shown on Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:SPPwater"

\end_inset

.
 Water can be excited by laser pulse and generate a high number of free-carriers
 (
\begin_inset Formula $N_{e}\sim3\times10^{22}$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $cm^{-3}$
\end_inset

).
 Indeed, the Kerr effect in water is ## times stronger than in air (
\begin_inset Formula $n_{2}^{water}=$
\end_inset

) and the number of carriers in valence band is not limited in the liquid
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "Noack1999,Vogel2002"

\end_inset

.
 
