 are a high density in the conduction band.
 This mode is found at sub-critical densities and would correspond to interferen
ces between propagated waves (radiation remnants ?).
 At lower thicknesses, the multilayer SPP calculations provide an interesting
 possible transition between the SPP mode and the propagation mode.
 The transition occurs at the critical density defined by 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
n_{cr}=\frac{m_{e}\varepsilon_{0}\Re e\left(\varepsilon_{\infty}\right)}{e^{2}}\left(\omega^{2}+\nu^{2}\right)\label{eq:CriticalDensity}
