 presents the simulation results performed considering the excitation of
 a layer of water between the ambient medium and the bulk Si.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:IsoLinesWater0WaterSi0"

\end_inset

 (a) demonstrates the SPP periodicity at the 
\begin_inset Formula $water-water^{*}$
\end_inset

 interface, and 
\begin_inset Formula $water^{*}-Si$
\end_inset

 interface.
 The 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

restricted
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 curves show the periodicities for which SPP are allowed to be excited regarding
 condition given by Eq.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand eqref
reference "eq:ConditionSPP"

\end_inset

.
 We first underline multilayer 
\begin_inset Formula $water-water^{*}-Si$
\end_inset

 system shows the same periodicity as SPP at single interface 
\begin_inset Formula $water-water^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 No low periodicity is observed for any layer thickness.
 However, the SPP at simple interface 
\begin_inset Formula $water^{*}/Si$
\end_inset

 reveals a periodicity of 105 nm near 
\begin_inset Formula $N_{e}\sim3\times10^{28}$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $m^{-3}$
\end_inset

.
 Vertical bar shows the critical density in water (
\begin_inset Formula $n_{cr}^{H_{2}O}=3.26\times10^{27}\, m^{-3}$
\end_inset

).
 
