\begin_layout Standard
Considering the excitation of water revealed that sensitive reduction of
 the SPP periodicity can be reached and must be investigated more deeply.
 Moreover, looking forward alternating nature of dielectric layers drive
 us to consider an oxide layer, which has been demonstrated as important
 after irradiation in water.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Interfaces involving oxide layer
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Following our path after finding that far subwavelength periodicities are
 possible if we consider excitation of water, we turn now to the study of
 SPP periodicity considering the presence of an oxide layer.
 We also compare the periodicities obtained in air medium with the one obtained
 in water medium, so for Ti and Si.
 
\end_layout

